summer is now at an end and it was a big  one for Hogwarts Legacy seems like news  is starting to slow down just a bit  giving all of us time to catch our  breath and recap all of the many  announcements that we've gotten over the  past several months but it certainly  doesn't sound like they're going to be  quiet for long Hogwarts Legacy Community  manager Chandler wood recently took to  Twitter to give a pretty big hint that  we are going to see some gameplay of  Hogwarts Legacy very soon he knows that  is something that fans have been asking  to see more of and personally I think  there are three big time questions still  remaining about Hogwarts Legacy and I  actually think an extended look at  gameplay might give us the answers to at  least two of them number one how does  time pass in Hogwarts Legacy okay I'm  kind of cheating with this one because  there are really multiple questions  rolled up into one here but I feel like  if we got an answer to how time passes  that would really give us some insight  into so much about how the rest of the  game is going to work more specifically  I'm thinking about classes here do we  have to be in class at a specific time  on a specific day or is it more of an  open-ended thing how do the day night  cycles work how does that work with the  various quests we're given along with  those classes that we just talked about  then there's the whole season system and  I know a lot of you think that Hogwarts  Legacy is going to be more than one  school year I still think it's just  going to be one single school year and  we'll get to see all four seasons in  that one school year but who knows  that's one where I would love to be  wrong on I think what's so interesting  about this one is that Avalanche really  has to make sure they strike that  balance between something that's fun to  play something that doesn't feel super  time sensitive like you're going to miss  a key deadline but then also with the  realism aspect I mean people want to  feel like they're actually taking  classes and going to school at Hogwarts  and one thing I think we have to keep in  mind here is that it's not an MMO as I  remind people time and time again it is  an action RPG so if you're looking at  realism and fun on a scale they're going  to go way more toward the fun side of  things than trying to keep things super  realistic which for some fans is  probably going to be disappointing but I  think most fans will be pretty pleased  by hearing that again that's just my  guess that we don't no we haven't seen  this yet in practice now another aspect  that is super interesting about the  classes is that they will certainly  impact the game's story in some way now  we've already even seen cutscenes for  the classes so we know we're not going  to get them every day is it every week  is it once a quarter is it just a  one-time thing you get a class are there  a couple spread out through the year can  you completely just ignore classes like  say you decide you know what I don't  really want to take potions I'm not  going to take potions a lot of people  still want to know can you skip classes  and if you do skip classes then what  happens as a result of that can you go  back and make that up or just completely  miss out on it now over the years of  video games who have tackled this  problem they've handled it in a number  of different ways on one side you have a  game like Animal Crossing which actually  uses a real world clock so if it's 8 am  in the real world it is 8 am in your  Animal Crossing or at least if it's 8 am  on your Nintendo switch so anything that  you have to do at night in Animal  Crossing you have to do at night in the  real world again unless you kind of  Tinker around with the switches settings  then you have a game like The Legend of  Zelda breath of the wild where the  weather is constantly changing the time  is constantly changing and then then  even within that you have the ability to  advance to a certain point of the day  and this system here is certainly how a  lot of games handle it however it could  be a little bit problematic for Hogwarts  Legacy because of the fact that we have  to take classes and the vast majority of  those classes take place during the  daytime hours so to summarize this one  here classes seasons and the day night  cycle they're each going to be  significant to how Hogwarts Legacy feels  to play and yet other than knowing that  all three are there and exist in the  game we actually know very little about  how these systems will work that's why  it's one of my three biggest questions  remaining moving on to number two how do  spells work in Hogwarts Legacy how many  can we have how do the finishers work  can you just Spam Avada Kedavra like  crazy now we have seen glimpses of  Hogwarts legacies HUD and plenty of the  spells in action what we haven't seen is  how we'll chain these spells together in  battle we saw from that PS5 trailer that  R2 is going to be involved somehow in  casting spells we also see the little  pop-ups in the Gameplay trailer that we  already have where R1 seems to be tied  to a pug nut know how many spells can we  have equipped at a given time and does  it all have to go on that Hut how do we  switch them in and out there's also been  quite a bit of talk among fans about the  possibility of a wheel of sorts but  we've actually seen nothing official at  all on that just yet what we do know is  that from watching the gameplay you can  chain these spells together very quickly  I mean in Rapid succession and while we  don't exactly know how many we know that  the trailers have mentioned dozens of  spells at a bare minimum and with me  being someone who is so keen on the  actual gameplay when it comes to video  games for me at least the story is  secondary I mean it's great if you have  an awesome story but we play games too  play games enjoy the actual gameplay if  I wanted to just sit and watch something  I could go watch a movie I could read a  book watch a TV show there are plenty of  other ways to get just a story but  that's what makes games so unique so  this is why to me the gameplay is so  crucial and I feel that spells and  combat how they all work together is  really going to go a long way to  determining how fun this game is to play  I have no doubt it's going to be an  absolute blast to explore I really do I  have no doubt about that whatsoever  there are going to be so many Secrets  packed in this game the adventure the  exploration is going to be top-notch  what I don't know and I just don't feel  we've seen enough yet is how the game's  gonna play and how fun it's going to be  moment to moment casting spells being in  the middle of combat upgrading all of  these things does it feel satisfying and  that is why this remains one of the  biggest questions that I still want to  know which takes us to number three who  is the Ravenclaw companion okay at first  I thought maybe I make this question is  there a rabbit claw companion but let's  be honest I mean it would be an  incredible shock if they do not include  a Ravenclaw companion I can't see them  doing that for the other three houses  but for some reason Ravenclaw is just  not included nah not happening don't see  it there is going to be a Ravenclaw  companion and this leads directly into a  follow-up question again kind of  cheating here but I gotta know why has  it been a secret for so long does this  Ravenclaw companion hold some  significance will we perhaps recognize  their last name are they from one of  those storied Wizarding World families  who we will just immediately know right  off the bat who this person is related  to I'll be honest I think it'd be  awesome I think it'd be really cool if  that were the case I think it's much  simpler than that though I think it's  more of a marketing thing I think it's  just something that Avalanche has  decided hey you know what this would be  something cool to hold and reveal later  on especially when they had to push the  game to 2023 obviously they want to have  plenty of things to kind of keep the  hype going keep the fandom talking and  one of the big cards that they are still  holding is the identity of this  Ravenclaw companion so I think it's just  something that they decided to hold back  on and then reveal at a later date now  there was some talk for a while as to  whether or not we'll have more than four  companions so we're thinking three that  we've already seen plus one other from  Ravenclaw so that'd be one from each  house and I just keep going back and  forth on this I mean we've seen our  character in battle with someone like  fig who I don't think fig will be an  actual companion to us but I could see a  number of different characters that we  meet throughout the game kind of joining  us for a time but then again I don't  know maybe that's what they mean by  companion it's anyway maybe the  companions are not going to stick with  us throughout the whole game and go with  us on every single Mission I guess I'm  thinking too much of something like  Persona here whereas instead perhaps  they're leaning more into the side of  hey these are just characters that you  meet throughout the game and if you  choose because we know that the missions  we've seen with Sebastian and natsai are  both Optical quests which is absolutely  incredible to still think that we've  only scratched the surface of everything  in this game is just amazing now if you  guys have enjoyed a couple of my videos  make sure you hit that subscribe button  before you go I can't thank you enough  for all your support as always thank you  all so much for watching I'll talk to  you again soon
 

